2. Axiomatic Foundation

Axiom 2.1 (Sigmoidal Cognitive Production)

For each content object i, the cognitive production function D_i : \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} satisfies:

(i) Smoothness. D_i \in \mathcal{C}^2(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}).

(ii) Boundary. D_i(0) = 0.

(iii) Strict Monotonicity. D_i'(A_i) > 0 for all A_i > 0.

(iv) Unique Inflection. There exists a unique A_{0,i} > 0 such that:

D_i''(A_i) > 0 \quad \text{for } A_i \in (0, A_{0,i})

D_i''(A_i) < 0 \quad \text{for } A_i \in (A_{0,i}, \infty)

D_i''(A_{0,i}) = 0

(v) Boundedness. \lim_{A_i \to \infty} D_i(A_i) = D_{\max,i} < \infty.

(vi) Vanishing Marginal Return. \lim_{A_i \to \infty} D_i'(A_i) = 0.

A canonical parametric form satisfying Axiom 2.1 is the logistic production function:

D_i(A_i) = \frac{D_{\max,i}}{1 + e^{-k_i(A_i - A_{0,i})}} - D_{0,i}

where D_{0,i} = \frac{D_{\max,i}}{1 + e^{k_i A_{0,i}}} ensures D_i(0) = 0.

Axiom 2.2 (Construct–Instrument Separation)

The latent constructs D(C) and A_h(C,u) are not identical to their estimators \widehat{D}(C) and \widehat{A}_h(C,u). In particular:

T(C,u) \neq A_h(C,u)

Exposure time is an observable proxy, not the construct.

Axiom 2.3 (Platform Independence)

The platform selection operator \mathcal{S}_p : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}_p is conditionally independent of latent cognitive depth D_i(A_i). Formally:

\mathcal{S}_p \perp D_i(A_i) \mid (V_i, T_i)

The platform filters on observable engagement signals, not on latent depth.

