A.11. Proof of Proposition A.1 (Empty-Set Case)

Statement. If E_i(A_i^\dagger) < \lambda_{\min} for all i, where \lambda_{\min} := \min_i E_i(A_i^\dagger), then the optimal allocation is A_i^* = 0 for all i.

Proof. By Theorem 3.4, any active item must satisfy A_i^* \geq A_i^\dagger. The minimum shadow price compatible with any activation is \lambda_{\min}. If no item attains E_i(A_i^\dagger) \geq \lambda_{\min}, then no item can be activated at a return exceeding the shadow price. The empty allocation is optimal. \blacksquare

