Appendix H: Dynamic Extension (v0.5 Preview)

H.1. Context-Dependent Depth

Definition H.1. D(C_i \mid \mathcal{H}_{u,t}) denotes cognitive depth conditional on user u's cognitive history \mathcal{H}_{u,t}.

Assumption H.2 (History Dependence). D(C_i \mid \mathcal{H}_{u,t}) is non-decreasing in the richness of \mathcal{H}_{u,t} for content C_i that builds on prior knowledge.

H.2. Dynamic Programming Formulation

The allocation problem becomes:

V_t(\mathcal{H}_t, B_t) = \max_{\{A_i\}} \left\{ \sum_i D_i(A_i \mid \mathcal{H}_t) + \beta V_{t+1}(\mathcal{H}_{t+1}, B_{t+1}) \right\}

subject to:

\sum_i A_i \leq B_t

\mathcal{H}_{t+1} = \mathcal{H}_t \cup \{(C_i, A_i)\}

H.3. Bellman Equation

Under standard regularity conditions (bounded returns, discount factor \beta \in (0,1)), the value function satisfies:

V_t(\mathcal{H}, B) = \max_{\{A_i\}} \left\{ \sum_i D_i(A_i \mid \mathcal{H}) + \beta \mathbb{E}\left[ V_{t+1}(\mathcal{H}', B') \mid \mathcal{H}, \{A_i\} \right] \right\}

The optimal policy is characterized by the first-order condition:

\frac{\partial D_i}{\partial A_i} + \beta \frac{\partial \mathbb{E}[V_{t+1}]}{\partial A_i} = \lambda_t

where \lambda_t is the shadow price of attention at time t.

